hadiths[51]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17189","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Raja informed me, he said: I heard Aws ibn Damaj, he said: I heard Abu Masud al-Ansari al-Badri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The people are led by the most reciting of them of the Book of Allah Most High, and the earliest of them in recitation. If their recitation is equal, let the earliest of them in emigration lead them. If their emigration is equal, let the eldest of them lead them. A man is not led among his family nor in his authority, nor is sat upon his honored seat in his house, except that he permits you, or except with his permission."
"17190","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik narrated to us, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, that a man was brought to by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and He said: What did you do in this world? The man said to Him: I did not do the weight of an atom of good I hope You with. He said it to Him three times, and said at the third: O Lord, You had given me surplus of wealth in this world, and I traded with the people, and of my character was to overlook, and I eased upon the well-off and gave time to the insolvent. He, Mighty and Majestic, said: We are more entitled to that than you. Overlook My servant. He was forgiven him. Abu Masud said: Thus I heard from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17191","And another man ordered his family when he dies to burn him, then grind him, then scatter him on a windy stormy day. They did that with him. He was gathered to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He said to him: What carried you to this? He said: O Lord, there was no servant more disobedient to You than me, and I hoped to escape. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Overlook My servant. He was forgiven him. Abu Masud said: Thus I heard it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17192","Yazid narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I lag in the dawn prayer fearing so-and-so, meaning their imam. He said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more angry in admonition than him that day. He said: O people, among you are repellers. Whichever prays with the people, let him lighten, for among them is the weak and the old and the needy."
"17193","Yazid informed us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd: Ismail narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointed with his hand toward Yemen and said: Faith is here. Nay, harshness and thickness of hearts are among the loud-voiced owners of camels, where the horn of Satan rises, in Rabiah and Mudar. Muhammad said: At the roots of the tails of camels."
"17194","Uthman ibn Umar informed us: Malik informed us, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Masud, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, and bless Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim among the worlds. You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"17195","I read this hadith upon Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Nuaym ibn Abd Allah, that Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed him, from Abu Masud."
"17196","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Alqamah, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever reads the two verses from the end of al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him."
"17197","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Thabit, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Qasim, or al-Qasim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Utbah, from Abu Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: This authority is among you, and you are its rulers, and it will remain among you until you innovate deeds. When you do that, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends upon you the worst of His creation, and they strip you as the stick is stripped."
"17198","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me that Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed him that he heard Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the price of a dog, and the dowry of a prostitute, and the gift of a soothsayer."
"17199","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah al-Dastuwai narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform witr at the first of the night and its middle and its last."
"17200","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me about sending blessings upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a Muslim man sends blessings upon him in his prayer, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbih al-Ansari, brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj, from Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr, he said: A man came until he sat before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we were with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, as for greeting upon you, we knew it, so how do we send blessings upon you when we pray in our prayer, Allah send blessings upon you? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell silent until we wished the man had not asked him. He said: When you send blessings upon me, say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad the unlettered Prophet and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad the unlettered Prophet as You blessed Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim. You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"17201","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Umara ibn Umayr al-Taymi narrating from Abu Ma'mar al-Azdi, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No prayer suffices for a man, or for anyone, who does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration."
"17202","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri said that Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham ibn al-Mughira narrated to him that Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the brother of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, who is the grandfather of Zayd ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib on his mother's side, narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade them the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"17203","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah, who is Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: It was said to him, What did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say about 'za'amu' [they allege]? He said: An evil mount for a man."
"17204","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, he said: Salim al-Barrad narrated to us, and he said: he was with me more trustworthy than myself, he said: Abu Mas'ud al-Badri said to us: Shall I not pray for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Then he said Allahu Akbar and bowed and placed his palms on his knees, and his fingers were spread apart over his shins, and he kept his arms away from his sides until everything of him settled, then he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, and stood upright until everything of him settled, then he said Allahu Akbar and prostrated and kept away from his sides until everything of him settled, then he raised his head and sat upright until everything of him settled, then he prostrated the second time, and he prayed with us four rak'as like this, then he said: Such was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray."
"17205","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Isma'il, that he heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrating from Abu Mas'ud, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so prolongs the prayer for us until I indeed stay behind, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became angry with an anger such as I never saw him angry in an admonition, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among you are those who repel, so whoever leads people let him lighten the prayer for them, for behind him are the old, the sick, and the one with a need."
"17206","Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Amir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with al-Abbas, his uncle, to the seventy of the Ansar at al-Aqaba under the tree, and said: Let your speaker speak and not prolong the sermon, for there is an eye of the idolaters upon you, and if they know of you they will expose you, so their speaker, who is Abu Umama, said: Ask, O Muhammad, for your Lord whatever you wish, then ask for yourself and your companions whatever you wish, then tell us what reward we have from Allah Almighty and from you if we do that, he said: Then he said: I ask you for my Lord Almighty that you worship Him and associate nothing with Him, and I ask you for myself and my companions that you shelter us and help us and defend us as you defend yourselves, they said: Then what is ours if we do that? He said: For you is Paradise, they said: Then that is yours."
"17207","Yahya ibn Zakariya narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, similar to this, he said: And Abu Mas'ud was the youngest of them in age."
"17208","Yahya ibn Zakariya narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: Neither the old nor the young heard a sermon like it."
"17209","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Salim Abu Abd Allah, he said: Uqba ibn Amr said: Shall I not show you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Then he stood and said Allahu Akbar, then bowed and kept his hands away and placed his hands on his knees and spread his fingers behind his knees until everything of him settled, then he raised his head and stood until everything of him settled, then he prostrated and kept away until everything of him settled, he said: Then he prayed four rak'as, then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray, or: thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray with us."
"17210","Affan narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrating from Abu Mas'ud, I said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When a Muslim spends maintenance on his family while seeking its reward, it is charity for him."
"17211","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man of those before you was reckoned and nothing of good was found for him except that he was a wealthy man and used to deal with people, and he used to say to his servants: Overlook the insolvent, he said: Then Allah Almighty said to His angels: We are more entitled to that than he, overlook him."
"17212","Ibn Numayr and Ya'la and Muhammad, meaning the two sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, they said: al-A'mash informed us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My mount has broken down with me, so carry me, he said: I have nothing to carry you on, but go to so-and-so, so he went to him and he carried him, then he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer, Muhammad said: For it has broken down with me."
"17213","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abu Mas'ud, from a man of the Ansar called Abu Shu'ayb, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I recognized hunger in his face, so I went to a servant of mine, a butcher, and ordered him to make food for us for five men, he said: Then I invited the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as the fifth of five, and a man followed them, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reached the door, he said: This one has followed us, if you wish to permit him, otherwise he will return, so he permitted him."
"17214","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My mount has broken down with me, that is I am cut off, so carry me, then he mentioned the hadith."
"17215","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: While I was beating a servant of mine I heard a voice behind me: Know, Abu Mas'ud, three times, so I turned and there was the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: By Allah, Allah is more able over you than you are over this one, he said: Then I swore never to beat a slave again."
"17216","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"17217","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: We were with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz and he once delayed the Asr prayer, so Urwa ibn al-Zubayr said to him: Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud al-Ansari narrated to me that al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba once delayed the prayer, meaning Asr, so Abu Mas'ud said to him: Indeed, by Allah, O Mughira, you have known that Jibril, peace be upon him, came down and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, and the people prayed with him, then he came down and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, and the people prayed with him, until he counted five prayers, so Umar said to him: Watch what you say, O Urwa, did Jibril himself establish the prayer? Urwa said: Thus Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud narrated to me, and Umar kept learning the prayer time by a sign until he left this world."
"17218","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash narrating from Abu Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Of what people have attained of the speech of the first prophethood: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"17219","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'ba informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: I used to narrate a hadith from Abu Mas'ud, then I met him while he was circumambulating the House, so I asked him, and he narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever recites the last two verses of Surat al-Baqara in a night, they suffice him."
"17220","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Raja, he said: I heard Aws ibn Dam'aj saying: I heard Abu Mas'ud saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: The people are led by the most reciting of them of the Book of Allah Almighty and the earliest of them in recitation, and if their recitation is equal then let the earliest of them in Hijra lead them, and if they are equal in Hijra then let the oldest of them lead them, and a man is not led in his family nor in his authority, nor is one seated on his honored seat in his house except with his permission, or by his permission."
"17221","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abu Mas'ud, that a man of his people called Abu Shu'ayb made food and sent to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Come to me, you and five with you, he said: So he sent back to him: Permit a sixth for me."
"17222","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Mas'ud, that a man gave charity of a bridled she-camel in the path of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will surely come on the Day of Resurrection with seven hundred bridled she-camels."
"17223","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman, from Alqama, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever recites the two verses of al-Baqara in a night, they suffice him, Abd al-Rahman said: Then I met Abu Mas'ud and he narrated it to me."
"17224","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqara in a night, they suffice him."
"17225","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Dam'aj, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people are led by the most reciting of them of the Book of Allah Almighty, and if they are equal in recitation then the most knowledgeable of them of the Sunna, and if they are equal in the Sunna then the earliest of them in Hijra, and if they are equal in Hijra then the oldest of them, and a man is not led in his authority, nor is one seated on his honored seat except with his permission."
"17226","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba and al-Thawri narrated to us, they said: Mansur narrated to us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: I heard Abu Mas'ud Uqba ibn Amr al-Badri saying: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Of what people have attained of the speech of the first prophethood: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"17227","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'ba, he said: Isma'il ibn Raja narrated to me, and Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ulayya, said: Shu'ba said: from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Dam'aj, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The people are led by the most reciting of them of the Book of Allah and the earliest of them in recitation, and if they are equal in recitation then the earliest of them in Hijra, and if they are equal in Hijra then the oldest of them, and a man is not led in his authority, Isma'il said: nor among his family, nor is one seated on his honored seat, Isma'il said: in his house, except by his permission, or he permits you."
"17228","Yahya and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17229","And Waki' said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Uqba ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqara in a night, they suffice him."
"17230","Isma'il and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il informed us, from Qays, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sun and moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone, Yazid said: nor for his life, but they are two signs of the signs of Allah Almighty, so when you see them, pray."
"17231","Waki' and Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, they said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umara ibn Umayr al-Taymi, from Abu Ma'mar Abd Allah ibn Sakhbara al-Azdi, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wipe our shoulders in prayer, Waki' said: and say: Straighten and do not differ, lest your hearts differ, let those of understanding and maturity be nearest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them, Abu Mas'ud said: So today you are more severely differing."
"17232","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr said: al-A'mash narrated to us, and Ibn Abi Za'ida, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umara ibn Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abu Mas'ud, Ibn Abi Za'ida said: al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No prayer suffices for anyone who does not straighten his back in it in bowing and prostration."
"17233","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman, he said: I heard Umara ibn Umayr, the like of it, he narrated to us."
"17234","Waki' from Sufyan, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, then he mentioned it."
"17235","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say He Allah the One equals a third of the Qur'an."
"17236","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Of what people have attained of the speech of the first prophethood: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"17237","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash narrating from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, then he mentioned the like of it."
"17238","Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in a night? Allah the One, the Eternal."
"17239","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Ansari narrating from Abu Mas'ud, Bahz said: al-Badri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: When a Muslim spends maintenance on his family while seeking its reward, it is charity for him."
